 "thumbnail": "the lid goes straight",
 "script": "What if you were ten times stronger? Not gym strong. Ten times. On Monday morning you twist open a pickle jar, and the lid goes straight through the ceiling. By lunch you've carried your neighbor's piano up four flights of stairs, with one hand, while texting. Everyone at school wants to arm wrestle you, and nobody even comes close. But then something weird starts happening. Every time you go all out, something cracks. Not the table. You. First a finger, then a rib. Because here's what nobody tells you: your muscles were never the weak part. Your brain is quietly holding them back, right now, because at full power they're strong enough to break your own bones. That's why people can break bones during a seizure. And your muscles just got ten times stronger, while your bones stayed exactly the same. So you learn to live at ten percent. Soft handshakes. Careful hugs. Until the day a car rolls back onto your little brother's leg, and the only way to lift it is one hundred percent. You know exactly what it'll cost you. You lift it anyway. Would you still want this power? Yes or no?",
